{"subject":"Pharmacology","sourceTitle":"All In One Online","title":"PrepLadder · 1.Previous Year Questions","deckName":"created by tele @Neet_pg_bot::prep::Qbank::Pharmacology::1.Previous_Year_Questions","questions":[{"id":"all-in-one-1760436534814","topic":"PrepLadder · 1.Previous Year Questions","number":1,"stem":"A drug solution containing 500 mg/5 ml of the drug is given to you. You are provided with a 2 ml syringe (having 10 divisions for each ml). How many divisions of the 2 ml syringe need to be administered to deliver 180 mg of the drug to a patient?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1.8"},{"label":"B","text":"10"},{"label":"C","text":"14"},{"label":"D","text":"18"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"18","solutionHtml":"<p><strong>Correct Option D. </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>To determine how many divisions of the 2 ml <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"29863704261692777199d30fdfa6fa\">syringe</span> need to be administered to deliver 180 mg of the drug, we need to calculate the volume of the drug solution that contains 180 mg of the drug.</li>\n<li>Given: Drug concentration: 500 mg/5 ml</li>\n<li>First, we can calculate the drug concentration per <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"84c61ff01716927771922502f2e373\">milliliter</span> (mg/ml): 500 mg / 5 ml = 100 mg/ml</li>\n<li>Next, we can calculate the volume of the drug solution needed to deliver 180 mg of the drug: 180 mg / 100 mg/ml = 1.8 ml</li>\n<li>Since the provided <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"29863704261692777199d30fdfa6fa\">syringe</span> has 10 divisions for each milliliter, we need to determine the number of divisions for 1.8 ml.</li>\n<li>Number of divisions = 1.8 ml * 10 divisions/ml = 18 divisions</li>\n<li>Therefore, 18 divisions of the 2 ml <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"29863704261692777199d30fdfa6fa\">syringe</span> need to be administered to deliver 180 mg of the drug to the patient.</li>\n</ul>\n<br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">.</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436534816","topic":"PrepLadder · 1.Previous Year Questions","number":2,"stem":"According to the Drugs and Cosmetics Rules, match the following medications with their corresponding schedules. Medication Schedule 1. Insulin A. Schedule H 2. Hepatitis B vaccine B. Schedule Z 3. Morphine C. Schedule G 4. Veterinary drugs D. Schedule X","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1-C, 2-D, 3-B, 4-A"},{"label":"B","text":"1-C, 2-A, 3-D, 4-B"},{"label":"C","text":"1-B, 2-A, 3-D, 4-C"},{"label":"D","text":"1-D, 2-B, 3-A, 4-C"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"1-C, 2-A, 3-D, 4-B","solutionHtml":"al-align:top\"&amp;gt;\n\t\t\t<p><strong>Medication </strong></p>\n\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Schedule</strong></p>\n</td>\n\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Insulin</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Schedule G</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Hepatitis B vaccine</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Schedule H</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Morphine</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Schedule X</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Veterinary drugs</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Schedule Z</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Schedules of drugs as per the Drugs and Cosmetics Act of India:</strong></p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:612px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Schedule</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Description</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Schedule C</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Biological and Special Products: Includes sera, vaccines, toxins, antitoxins, insulin, etc.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Schedule D</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Drugs: Extends to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"552e9ef8811692777186997018b858\">diagnostic</span> kits and reagents including various biotechnological products.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Schedule E</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Substances: Includes toxic substances such as poisonous plants and their preparations.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Schedule F</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Vaccines and Sera: Specifies standards for blood products and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"552e9ef8811692777186997018b858\">diagnostic</span> antigens.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Schedule G</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Prescription Drugs: Drugs that should be taken under medical supervision only and must carry a warning.</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Schedule H</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Prescription Only Drugs: Sale restricted to prescription from a registered medical practitioner.</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Schedule J</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Diseases: List of diseases for which medicines cannot claim to cure or treat, such as cancer, AIDS, etc.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Schedule O</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Disinfectants and Insecticides</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Schedule R</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Standards for Cosmetics: Specifies standards for soaps, shampoos, creams, etc.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Schedule W</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Drugs marketed under <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"343b03419d169277718828bb100c95\">generic</span> names.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Schedule X</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Narcotic and Psychotropic Substances</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Schedule Y</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Requirement and guidelines for import/manufacture or Clinical trials in India</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">KDT - Essentials of Medical Pharmacology, 8th Edition, Page 7.<br/>1 Centre for Science and Environment recommendations: Modifications in Drugs and Cosmetics Act (1940) and Rules (1945)<br/>The Drugs and Cosmetics Act and Rules</div>","tags":""}]}